WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.200
I'm glad to see you again, Yuu.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.440
A heartwarming reunion...

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.650
Or maybe not?

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.240
You've been with us this whole time.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.530
It really wasn't so bad.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.530
It was always lively.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.780
I'm a little disappointed that I 
have to go back to being alone.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:46.110
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.080
I won't let you have Tear.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.510
<b>Unlimited Fafnir</b>

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.570
I won't let her become a Basilisk's mate!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.600
Nitro Bullet!

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.670
You people seem to think that 
the only two options are

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.890
to defeat the Basilisk or to let Tear die.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.450
But maybe she has a future living as a Dragon.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.950
To hell with that.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.960
Would she be better off 
dead than being a Dragon?

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.990
Really?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.630
Is there anything worse than being dead?

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.350
There might not be.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.100
But it's up to us, ourselves, 
to decide what's important.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.630
And Tear has chosen to be a human.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.400
I won't give her to the likes of you.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.710
Fine.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.070
I'll stop if you can kill me.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.950
Anti-explosive armor Urk 73E!

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.880
Laevateinn!

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.260
D or not,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.830
if they're human, you won't lose.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.600
My Fafnir.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.190
What's the matter?

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:08.480
Kill me.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.490
Tear chose to live as a human.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.330
What do you want to do?

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.280
Like I said, I'm a Dragon.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.030
But you also told me to choose for you.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.660
I think of you as a human.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.870
Why?

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.830
Because I thought I could kill you.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.280
I see.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.200
You've decided that I'm a human.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.640
Kili.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.910
I'll let you have Tear back.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.860
But the Basilisk is formidable.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.810
I think it's seen the future.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.180
The future?

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:10.270
Show me that you're a better 
man than the Basilisk.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.090
Tear-san!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.480
She's fine.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.920
Quickly, to the sick bay.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.610
Honoka-chan was...

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.010
The Basilisk has seen the future?

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:43.280
Honoka-san... I mean, Kili really said that?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.150
Yeah.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:48.940
Then the incredible precognitive 
ability it used against NIFL

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.040
and at the island makes sense.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:52.870
Yeah.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.840
Why, Honoka-chan?

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.070
We were together all this time.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.330
Even at the hot springs.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.450
Was it all a lie?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.670
Iris...

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.890
I'll be going over the plan one more time.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.980
The Mistilteinn drop height 
will be 15,000 meters.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.570
We'll move to the drop site on a 
large carrier provided by NIFL.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:35.660
Fyril-san and I will be in charge of 
controlling the Mistilteinn's drop.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.060
It will be difficult to control its trajectory

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.760
once it's taken the Catastrophe attack.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.590
We'll have to maintain position

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.800
I could get hooked on this!

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:51.180
above the Basilisk at all times using sensor data.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.080
Yeah, I can do it.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.890
I'm good with elaborate controls.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:59.970
In anticipation of the Basilisk 
making evasive maneuvers,

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.070
we will control its drop 
until just before impact.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.910
We will retreat five seconds before impact.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:10.130
But this will make it difficult 
to escape from the explosion.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.870
Therefore, we will ask Ariela-san to 
deploy multiple physical barriers.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.120
Leave it to me.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.790
Lisa-san and Ren-san, 
along with Fyril-san and I,

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.460
will do what we can to deploy an air barrier.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:29.620
This will surely hold back the explosion.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:34.760
And the two of you will be in charge of 
dealing with irregular circumstances.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.210
Irregular?

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.680
The event in which the third eye 
attack exceeds five seconds.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.400
If the attack exceeds 
five consecutive seconds,

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:44.740
respond with Plan A.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.550
If it discharges a second time, Plan B.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.240
If it takes evasive maneuvers,

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.360
please respond with Plan C.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:54.400
Okay.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.630
That'll decide whether we all live or die.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.790
We have the most crucial role.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.720
I understand.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.540
Watch as I complete it with perfection.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:10.960
I pray your plan will meet my expectations.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.760
Finally, Nii-san and Iris-san.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:19.270
What you do will depend 
largely on the circumstances.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.680
Do you remember all the patterns?

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.520
Yeah, I'm all set. Probably.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.330
"Probably" means you're not set at all.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.230
Uh...

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:33.580
It's all right. I'll take the lead.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.450
Okay, Nii-san,

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.910
please take care of your partner, Iris-san.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.330
Just wait.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.960
We'll take out the Basilisk for you, Tear.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.780
The Basilisk has stopped.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.120
Three minutes until drop.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:23.830
It must have noticed.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.630
<i>All units have completed their descents.</i>

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:29.080
The Basilisk stopped moving.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.340
It seems to have noticed the Mistilteinn.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.550
In three minutes, we'll arrive 
above the Basilisk and drop.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:36.870
Understood.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:49.860
Drop!

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.570
Drop initiated.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.290
Igniting altitude control thrusters.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.970
Altitude: 14,000 meters.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.050
No signs of evasive maneuvers 
from the Basilisk.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:17.430
<i>Readjusting trajectory.</i>

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.560
Passed the 12,000 meter mark.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.230
The Basilisk is changing its posture.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.290
It appears to be preparing 
to intercept the Mistilteinn.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.820
<i>Approaching altitude 10,000 meters.</i>

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:58.720
It's coming.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.890
The third eye is attacking!

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.150
We're separating from the Mistilteinn.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.350
Count five!

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.310
Four, three...

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.510
Iris!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.820
Two, one, zero.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.220
Just as predicted.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.470
Our calculations were right.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.070
But...

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.890
Ideally, we would have hoped for the 
attack to come after 5,000 meters.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.790
Be ready for a second 
discharge of the third eye.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.730
It might have used it early

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:34.600
to buy time to charge up for a second shot.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.630
That might be.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.090
Altitude now below 5,000 meters.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:42.050
It should be attacking with 
the standard Catastrophe now.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.620
Altitude: 2,000 meters.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.270
No sign of evasive maneuvers 
from the Basilisk.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.300
We won't hold out if the 
third eye attacks again.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.530
Second discharge approaching!

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.760
If the Basilisk is acting in 
response to the future it saw,

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.380
that's evidence that actions 
can change the future.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:28.260
Then we must change our own futures, as well.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.080
Initiating Plan B.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.460
We will be the second arrow.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.990
Let's go, Ren-san!

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.000
Too late!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.280
You're not getting away!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.330
There is no future for you!

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.560
Anti-gravity!

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:16.880
Aero Blast Quartet!

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.190
Mjolnir!

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.820
Seigin, burst!

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.370
Anti-Dragon armament, Marduke!

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.860
Offering: strength.

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:41.600
Seeking: destruction.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.060
This time...

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:03.580
This time, I'm going to protect it all!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.190
Megiddo, fire!

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:20.500
Final arrow: Last Quark!

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:05.500
It's gone. There isn't a trace of it left.

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:08.900
I'm told that Tear-san's Ryumon color faded,

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.760
and she's recovered.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.680
We did it.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.520
And everyone survived.

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.130
You've cleared all my conditions.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.480
Our promise.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.670
Mononobe Mitsuki-san,

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:33.110
I forgive you.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.390
You do?

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.030
But...

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.410
Jeez, you're such a pain.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.750
Mitsuki-san,

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.370
you've worked hard enough already.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.340
I admire you from the bottom of my heart.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:54.040
I'm proud to be your friend,

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.840
and I love you as my family.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.220
Thank you, Lisa-san.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.850
Mononobe, us, too.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:13.890
Huh?

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:15.290
One, two...

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.540
Mononobe Yuu, what are you doing?

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.270
Victory should be celebrated with everyone.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.820
Nii-san.

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:22.000
Yeah.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.160
I was forced into it!

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.780
Congratulations on defeating the Basilisk!

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.190
All right! We won!

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.570
Congrats!

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.670
We did it!

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.890
I'm told that the Basilisk has 
successfully been defeated.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.410
Yeah.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.310
You did it, huh?

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:49.630
That's my Fafnir.

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:56.800
You really did it, Yuu.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.150
We'll meet again.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:16.300
My chaste maidens are coming back!

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.960
It's a banquet tonight.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.430
A huge banquet of fun and flirting!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.260
You need to calm down.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:39.760
Are you going out?

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:43.200
Yeah. What's up?

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.260
Nii-san,

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:50.060
thank you for everything you did

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:52.230
in regards to Lisa-san.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:53.910
Nah,

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:56.870
you were the one who acted on it.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.840
Still, I'm thankful.

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:03.580
I know now that it's wrong to give up

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.280
on something for your own sake.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:07.890
So...

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.130
So...

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:16.860
I've decided not to give up on you, either.

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:18.360
Me?

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.360
Our promise as kids.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:25.790
My feelings back then, when I promised that

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:30.380
I'd love you more than anyone else forever.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.600
"Back then"?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.730
The day

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.590
we became siblings.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.610
My feelings will never change.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.630
I just wanted you to know that.

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.640
Sorry, I'm late.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.170
Mononobe!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.140
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:33.060
Nah, I wasn't waiting that long.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:38.820
Your memories?

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:41.070
Yeah.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:46.150
About when we met, too?

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:47.970
I remember.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.500
But...

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.060
Every time I make a trade with the Yggdrasil,

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.010
I lose memories.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:03.930
If I ever need more strength than I have now,

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.740
I'll make another trade.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:08.400
If that happens,

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.390
I might forget about you, too.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:12.860
So...

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.220
It's okay.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.400
Tell me about all your precious memories

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:38.910
that you don't want to forget.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:45.590
I'll remember them, so it'll be 
all right if you do forget.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.930
You will?

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.770
I won't ever forget you as you are now.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.220
I'll always be with you.

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:07.560
Nii-san, hurry up.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:08.530
We'll be late.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.510
It's fine.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:12.770
We'll make it by the opening chime.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:13.750
That's not good enough.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:18.510
I'd be setting a bad example 
as the student council president

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.670
if I barely arrived at school in time.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.170
Hey...

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.210
Yuu!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.050
Good morning.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.740
Morning, Tear.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.000
Good morning, Tear-san.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:34.100
Good morning.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.730
Morning.

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.560
It's a nice morning.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.020
Good morning.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.250
Good morning, Mononobe Yuu.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:47.700
You didn't arrive just in 
the nick of time, for once.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.480
I-I'm sorry!

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:56.020
Good morning, everyone.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.620
You're all here.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.840
Morning, Iris.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.490
Morning, Mononobe.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:50.070
<b>Illustration: Kabako</b>
